# ZBrain cross-platform line-ending policy
#
# Every crate's `lib.rs` is the entry point and follows the Windows CRLF
# convention. Without an explicit attribute, git relies on `text=auto`
# heuristics that produce *different* outcomes on different OSes (a file
# committed on Windows lands as CRLF everywhere; one committed on Linux
# lands as LF everywhere). That asymmetry has historically caused agents
# on different machines to "fight" the same file (one side's edit flips
# the worktree, the next side's commit produces an N/N full-file churn
# in `git diff --numstat`).
#
# The fix: explicitly pin every lib.rs to CRLF regardless of who/where
# committed it. Storage stays LF (`text=auto` below keeps the repo
# canonical), but every checkout, on every OS, by every agent, gets
# CRLF in the worktree. That removes the asymmetry at the root.
#
# Note: git patterns are evaluated bottom-up, so the more specific lines
# below must come AFTER the catch-all. We list each crate's lib.rs
# explicitly (no `**/lib.rs` glob — git's `**` matching is fragile across
# versions, and explicitness is cheap with 7 entries).
crates/zbrain-chunking/src/lib.rs text eol=crlf
crates/zbrain-cli/src/lib.rs text eol=crlf
crates/zbrain-core/src/lib.rs text eol=crlf
crates/zbrain-mcp/src/lib.rs text eol=crlf
crates/zbrain-svg/src/lib.rs text eol=crlf
crates/zbrain-web/src/lib.rs text eol=crlf
crates/zbrain-worker/src/lib.rs text eol=crlf
# All other text files: normalize repo storage to LF, checkout per-OS.
* text=auto
